20
00:00:59,942 --> 00:01:01,205
Here's the idea.

21
00:01:01,205 --> 00:01:05,101
We split the frame into patches, and every patch becomes a sensor.

22
00:01:05,101 --> 00:01:10,313
For each one, OpenCV 5 measures motion smaller than a twentieth of a pixel, frame by frame,

23
00:01:10,313 --> 00:01:14,525
and turns it into a frequency, an amplitude and a signal-to-noise ratio.

24
00:01:14,525 --> 00:01:18,157
One video, forty-eight sensors, nothing wired to the machine.

25
00:01:19,358 --> 00:01:23,518
Then an agent decides what to measure next, based on what it just measured.

26
00:01:23,518 --> 00:01:27,978
